# Nim build output
nimcache/
*.o
/apps/api/src/kori
/out/

# apps/web/dist is committed on purpose: the CI drift check compares it against a fresh
# `vite build`, and a plain `nim c` embeds it without needing node.

# Real env files live on qouver1 only (/srv/qouver/apps/kori/env/, mode 600).
ops/env/*.env
!ops/env/*.env.example
# The real provider config belongs on the host (mode 600), never in the repo; the committed
# template next to this line is the shape and carries placeholders only. The wildcard also covers
# config.json.tmp.<pid>, the copy a killed run leaves in the same directory.
ops/etc/config.json*
!ops/etc/config.json.example

# Deploy state written on the host
.deployed_rev

# Node
node_modules/

# macOS noise
.DS_Store
nimble.develop
nimble.paths
nimbledeps
# Generated by nimble on the first build ("begin Nimble config (version 2)"); never hand-edited.
# Only the copy nimble drops at the repo root. apps/api/src/config.nims is hand-written,
# tracked, and adds -d:ssl plus the revision define, so a bare pattern must never cover it.
/config.nims
